    "teach_3": {
      "id": "teach_3",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The age gap stays the same. A parent who is 24 years older will still be 24 years older four years later.\n\nLet child = c today. Parent = c + 24 today.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_3_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_3_step": {
      "id": "teach_3_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Four years later:\nChild = c + 4\nParent = c + 28.\n\nIf the parent is twice the child then, c + 28 = 2(c + 4). So c = 20 and parent = 44 today. Check future ages 24 and 48. The fixed gap helps us use just one unknown.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_3"
        }
      ]
    },
