    "teach_4": {
      "id": "teach_4",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A times-as-old clue in the past uses the same timeline. Suppose an older person is twice a child's age now.\n\nNow: child x, older 2x.\nSix years ago: child x − 6, older 2x − 6.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_4_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_4_step": {
      "id": "teach_4_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "If the older person was three times the child's age:\n2x − 6 = 3(x − 6)\n2x − 6 = 3x − 18\nx = 12.\n\nToday: 12 and 24. Six years ago: 6 and 18; 18 = 3 × 6. Check that the past child age is possible.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_4"
        }
      ]
    },
